# No trailing slash on node_modules: in a git worktree it is a SYMLINK to the main
# checkout's copy (installing per worktree would cost a full node_modules each), and
# "node_modules/" matches a directory but not a symlink — so the slash form left it
# showing as untracked, one `git add -A` away from being committed.
node_modules
dist/
.env
*.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store

# Per-machine Claude Code config, and the worktrees it creates for parallel work on
# separate pages. Both live inside the repo, so without this a session running
# `git add -A` would commit another session's entire working checkout.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/

# One-off investigation scripts (tmp-cols.ts, tmp-overlap.ts, tmp-denisa.ts, …). Seven of them were
# committed on this branch and carried for three days before being noticed: they are written against
# the live lake to answer one question, then dead. Ignored so the next one cannot ride along in a
# `git add -A`; anything worth keeping belongs in src/ with a test, not a tmp- prefix.
tmp-*.ts

# Same reasoning, different drawer: .scratch/ holds ad-hoc query runners pointed at the live lake
# (q.mts, an 11-line mssql harness for spot-checks). Useful and worth keeping on disk, but it is
# scaffolding rather than the product, and it was sitting one `git add -A` away from being committed.
.scratch/
